# This working tree is an Obsidian vault; the GitHub repo is only the code.
#
# The rule is an allowlist: everything at the root is ignored, and the few paths
# below are added back. A deny-list would need editing every time a draft, a
# result dump or a set of notes lands in the vault, and forgetting once publishes
# it. This way anything new is private until it is named here.
#
# Tracked: the code, the bibliography, and the two files that describe them.
# Untracked: the vault (papers, pdfs, reading notes, topics), the planning and
# handoff documents, thesis drafts, diagnostic write-ups, cluster output and
# every PDF.

/*

!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/README.md
!/refs.bib
!/code/

# Inside code/, the same split as before: source and run records are tracked,
# downloaded data and generated figures are not.

# Downloaded datasets. `/*` not `/`: a trailing slash excludes the directory and
# git does not descend into it, so the negation below would never match.
code/data/*
!code/data/imagenet100_wnids_*.json

# Run records are tracked; figures are not.
code/results/*
!code/results/*.json

# The reproduction sweeps are withheld until the model and class-subset control
# closes. Last match wins in this file, so these lines must stay below the
# allowlist above. The files exist locally; restore them by deleting this block.
code/results/gate_a_*.json
code/results/table2_by_rule.json
code/results/pilot20full_analysis.json
code/results/shards/

# Model weights and experiment scratch.
checkpoints/
runs/
wandb/
outputs/
*.pth
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.npy
*.npz

# Python.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# PDFs are never tracked. They are immutable downloads git cannot diff, and the
# paper set is reconstructible from refs.bib.
*.pdf

# OS cruft.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
